%N A402040 Decimal expansion of a self-referential continued fraction whose partial quotients are earlier convergents.
%C A402040 Let p(n)/q(n) be the convergents of 1 + 1/(1 + 2/(1 + 4/(3 + 20/(13 + 340/(229 + ...))))), i.e., 1/1, 2/1, 4/3, 20/13, 340/229, 84660/56861, ...
%C A402040 The partial numerators are 1, 2, 4, 20, 340, ... (A402041) and the partial denominators are 1, 1, 3, 13, 229, ... (A402042); each layer reuses the previous convergent p/q as numerator p and denominator q.
%C A402040 Recurrence: p(n) = p(n-1)*(q(n-1) + p(n-2)), q(n) = q(n-1)^2 + p(n-1)*q(n-2), with p(-1) = p(0) = 1, q(-1) = 0, q(0) = 1.
%e A402040 1.488869067977066594121068571592505436354535296007033...
%t A402040 Block[{P={1,1},Q={0,1},pn,qn},Do[pn=Q[[-1]]*P[[-1]]+P[[-1]]*P[[-2]]; qn=Q[[-1]]^2+P[[-1]]*Q[[-2]]; AppendTo[P, pn]; AppendTo[Q, qn],{14}]; RealDigits[N[P[[-1]]/Q[[-1]], 100]][[1]]]
%o A402040 (Python)
%o A402040 from decimal import Decimal, getcontext
%o A402040 getcontext().prec = 120
%o A402040 p0, p1, q0, q1 = 1, 1, 0, 1
%o A402040 for _ in range(14):
%o A402040     p0, p1, q0, q1 = p1, q1*p1 + p1*p0, q1, q1*q1 + p1*q0
%o A402040 print(str(Decimal(p1)/Decimal(q1))[:101])
%Y A402040 Cf. A402041, A402042.
%K A402040 nonn,cons,new
%O A402040 1,2
%A A402040 _Jason Bard_, Nov 11 2026
